Subject: Register bundles: register-keyed pc2line and frame ip

What this does
  Register bundles: register-keyed pc2line and frame ip.

Why we need it
  A register frame reports a register exec offset but the compiler's pc2line table is keyed by stack pc, so every register frame printed `(missing)`.

What it adds
  `regvm_build_pc2line` rebuilds the table for register offsets; `JSStackFrame.regvm_ip` captures the ip at every call/construct/apply/unwind boundary; `regvm_frame_pc` wired into both `build_backtrace` paths.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes - debug section is now register-keyed.
